Test Case: template_public_ip
================================================================================

Initial Error:
Error: Attempt to get attribute from null value
  on azapi.tf line 47, in resource "azapi_resource" "this":
  47:       type         = identity.value.type
    ├────────────────
    │ identity.value is null
This value is null, so it does not have any attributes.

Fix Process:

Attempt 1:
- Problem Analysis: Error "Attempt to get attribute from null value" in dynamic identity block at line 47. The for_each condition uses `can(module.replicator.azapi_header.identity)` which returns true even when the value is null, resulting in [null] being iterated.
- Fix Method: Update the identity dynamic block to match working pattern from previous successful test cases. Use `!= null` check instead of `can()`, and properly handle userAssignedIdentities.
- Changes Made:
  * Line 45: Changed `can(module.replicator.azapi_header.identity)` to `module.replicator.azapi_header.identity != null`
  * Line 48: Changed `try(identity.value.identity_ids, null)` to `try(identity.value.userAssignedIdentities, null) != null ? keys(identity.value.userAssignedIdentities) : null`
- Result: Success! Plan now runs without errors and shows acceptable drift.

Final Result for Step 3: Fix successful

